    {
      "id": "SCdBwFzuowdjvebiEUV_S",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1523.579365079365,
      "y": 219.38888888888863,
      "width": 989.29931640625,
      "height": 575,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0I",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 252716386,
      "version": 1309,
      "versionNonce": 960210355,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1787602816652,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Gradient Descent:\n- optimization algorithm\n- method use to find the best parameters of a ML model by minimizing a cost function\n\nGOAL: find the values of parameters that minimize the cost fun J(w,b)\n-not limited to linear regression. widely use to train neural networks, deep learning models\n- for a MODEL with MANY PARAMETERS: \n    - parameters could be w1, w2, …, wn b\n    - the goal is to find values  that give the SMALLEST possible J.\n- starting pint: \n    -choose initial values for the parameters\n    - for linear regression, a common choice is: w=0, b=0\n- HOW GRADIENT DESCENT WORKS:\n    1- Start at an initial point.\n    2- Determine the direction of steepest descent (the direction that decreases the cost fastest).\n    3- Take a small step downhill.\n    4- Repeat the process.\n    5- Eventually reach a minimum where the cost is as small as possible.\nNOTE: Gradient Descent = start somewhere --> find the steepest downhill direction --> take a \n                                    small step --> repeat until you reach a minimum\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Gradient Descent:\n- optimization algorithm\n- method use to find the best parameters of a ML model by minimizing a cost function\n\nGOAL: find the values of parameters that minimize the cost fun J(w,b)\n-not limited to linear regression. widely use to train neural networks, deep learning models\n- for a MODEL with MANY PARAMETERS: \n    - parameters could be w1, w2, …, wn b\n    - the goal is to find values  that give the SMALLEST possible J.\n- starting pint: \n    -choose initial values for the parameters\n    - for linear regression, a common choice is: w=0, b=0\n- HOW GRADIENT DESCENT WORKS:\n    1- Start at an initial point.\n    2- Determine the direction of steepest descent (the direction that decreases the cost fastest).\n    3- Take a small step downhill.\n    4- Repeat the process.\n    5- Eventually reach a minimum where the cost is as small as possible.\nNOTE: Gradient Descent = start somewhere --> find the steepest downhill direction --> take a \n                                    small step --> repeat until you reach a minimum\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
